            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for a butterfly, then the Sanskrit for a rooster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सारसः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सारसः — sārasaḥ — \"a crane\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sārasa is built from saras \"a lake, a pond\" (CDIAL 13359): first \"belonging to a lake\", then the Indian crane (MW). Hindi and Marathi kept it as sāras \"crane\" (CDIAL 13359)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
