          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kapola \"the cheek\" is probably borrowed from Austroasiatic, or possibly from Dravidian, as CDIAL 2755 reports after EWA; DEDR 1337 sets it, with a query mark, beside a Dravidian word for the cheek. Pali kept it as kapola (CDIAL 2755)."
            }
          ]
