        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "maṇibandha is built from maṇi \"jewel, bead\" and bandha \"tying\": the wrist is where jewels are tied on (MW). DEDR 4673 points out that the Dravidian word for the wrist, Kannada maṇikaṭṭu, is built the same way, and takes bandha as a translation of its kaṭṭu \"tie\"."
            }
          ]
        },
